-- title:
--   Supersingular regular prolongation with smooth-point charts at full level q
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and $M' \ge 1$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, with residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in `ssJSet q κ`), let $s \in W$, assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` such that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0$'s valuation subring and has $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Then there are a field $F_{ss}$, a $\kappa$-algebra structure on it, and a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F_{ss}$ with: (i) $F_{ss}/\kappa$ admits a transcendental element; (ii) for every $f$ in $R_0$'s integers that is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` where the $q$-expansion of $j$ is regular and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $R$'s integers and has $R$-residue the image in $F_{ss}$ of the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue; (iii) $R$'s integers are invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for all $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and (iv) there are a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ with $\#N = q+1$ and, for each place $Q$ of $F_{ss}/\kappa$, a subring $S_Q \subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'`, a ring map $\varphi_Q : A[X] \to S_Q$, a ring map $\chi_{0,Q} : S_Q \to \kappa$ and a set $D_Q$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that for every $Q \notin N$: $S_Q$ contains the image of $A$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_Q$ sends constants $a$ to the image of $a$ and $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$, while $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(X)) = 0$; for each $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ there is exactly one ring map $\chi : S_Q \to A$ fixing constants, lifting $\chi_{0,Q}$ modulo the maximal ideal, and with $\chi(\varphi_Q(X)) = c$; every $f \in S_Q$ lies in $R$'s integers, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue of that in $Q$'s residue field is the image of $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ has order $1$ at $Q$; $D_Q$ consists precisely of the rational places $P$ with $S_Q$ contained in $P$'s valuation subring, all values $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ on $S_Q$ in $A$, and $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) < 1$ exactly when $\chi_{0,Q}(f) = 0$; every $\chi : S_Q \to A$ fixing constants and lifting $\chi_{0,Q}$ arises from a unique $P \in D_Q$ via $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$; for $P \in D_Q$ the valuation subring of $P$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in S_Q$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h) \ne 0$; a nonzero $f$ of order $0$ at all $P \in D_Q$ becomes a unit of $S_Q$ after multiplication by a nonzero constant; and any $f$ in $R$'s integers lying in all valuation subrings of $D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$. Moreover distinct $Q, Q' \notin N$ have disjoint $D_Q, D_{Q'}$; for $Q \notin N$ every $P \in D_Q$ has non-negative order at the image of the $q$-expansion of $j$; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $R$'s integers, the induced residue automorphism `R.resAut τ` preserves $N$ and satisfies $\{P \mid \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D_Q\} = D_{\,\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q}$ for $Q \notin N$.
--
--   This is the valuation-theoretic packaging of the supersingular (Drinfeld) component of the semistable model at $q$ of the geometric component of the full level-$q$ modular curve over $X_0(M')$: the prolongation $R$ is the Gauss ring of that component, $N$ records its $q+1$ ends where the Igusa components are attached, and for each remaining point the data $(S_Q, \varphi_Q, \chi_{0,Q}, D_Q)$ give an étale coordinate together with its residue disc. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularChart_local`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularChart_local) to assemble the component chart at a supersingular place $s$.
